{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791667771,"nonce":"uLGl2M+9ShrrkqZ1c1N9kvWo9Lw=","message":"Input method placement landed in 495028e: while an editable text field has focus the host tells host.inputArea the caret's rectangle as it shows (window units, following scroll); mount sets it to the window's setImeAllowed and setImeCursorArea, so the input method is on only while text has focus and is off again on blur, removal, read-only or disabled. Nothing called setImeAllowed before, so a mounted window's input method was never turned on; this is verified only with a fake window, not with a real input method on the Mac. Also fixed on the way: a text field removed from the tree but not destroyed made the laid-out hook read bounds of an unlaid node and throw (HostNode.isConnected added). Left on this issue: select events and undo and redo.","files":null}]}